{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_repository_abstraction", "label": "Repository Abstraction Swap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Switching deps.py from SimulatedServoRepository to BridgeServoRepository changes nothing above that line: services, API, GUI and every test stay as they are. That swap is the whole point of the abstraction.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_simulatedservorepository", "label": "SimulatedServoRepository", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": null, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_bridgeservorepository", "label": "BridgeServoRepository", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": null, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_run_dev_entrypoint", "label": "run_dev.py Dev-PC Entrypoint", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Exists because two imports only live on the board (arduino.app_utils and possibly Logger461). It points DB_PATH and LOG_FILE at local files, then boots the app the way main.py does minus the Bridge relay.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_env_board_manual_step", "label": ".env.board Copy Is The Only Manual Step", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Forgetting it is silent: without .env, use_hardware_servo defaults to false, the backend runs the simulator, and the UI moves convincingly while the real servo never twitches. It is not shipped as .env because a dev machine would then drive hardware during pytest.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_adb_push_wipe_first", "label": "Wipe Before adb push", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "adb push overwrites files it copies but does not delete anything already on the board that is missing from the source, so renamed or deleted files linger and can be picked up instead of the new ones.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_bench_measured_settings", "label": "Bench-Measured Settings", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Every configured value came from the diagnostic app on real hardware, not a datasheet.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_no_modulus_wrapping", "label": "No Modulus-360 Wrapping", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "In a multi-turn system -25 and 335 degrees are different absolute targets a whole output revolution apart, and wrapping would hide turn-count errors.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_timestamp_not_ts", "label": "timestamp Never ts", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Renamed everywhere: entities, schemas, DB columns, CSV first column, query params and tests. Descriptive naming over abbreviation.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_angle_fault_flag", "label": "angle_fault Status Flag", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Sixth fault flag from status register bit 4, added end-to-end: entity, schema, /state, DB plus migration, CSV contract and GUI tile.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_multi_turn", "label": "Multi-Turn Support", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Not needed at plus/minus 90 degrees but kept because it is bench-proven: configure_range() applies angle limits 0, angle-resolution amplification and phase BIT4. Widening travel later is two numbers in .env, not a code change.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_core_version_pin", "label": "Pin The arduino:zephyr Core Version", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Board Manager does not exist on the air-gapped machine, so the target must already have arduino:zephyr at the version built against (0.56.0 or newer, which adds Serial3 and the UNO Q main-thread-priority fix). Most likely cause of 'it worked on my laptop'.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_check_bridge_contract", "label": "check_bridge_contract.py", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Every function crossing the MCU/Linux boundary is declared twice and nothing makes the compiler or interpreter compare them. A wrong argument count compiles and imports cleanly on both sides and fails at runtime as silence. Non-zero exit so it can go in a pre-commit hook.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_ethernet_patch_survival_check", "label": "Verify The Ethernet Patch Survived", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "~/.arduino15/internal/ is a user-global cache shared by every app. Three or more matches for IPAddress((uint32_t) means the patch is intact; zero means App Lab re-fetched the library and it must be re-applied.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_backend_liveness_check", "label": "Confirm Which Backend Is Live", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Two ways: the system health endpoint reports servo_backend, and the Python tab logs it at startup with a warning if simulated.", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_repository_abstraction", "target": "readme_simulatedservorepository", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_repository_abstraction", "target": "readme_bridgeservorepository", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_bridgeservorepository", "target": "sketch_readme_csv_payload_contract", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_env_board_manual_step", "target": "readme_simulatedservorepository", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_env_board_manual_step", "target": "readme_backend_liveness_check", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_env_board_manual_step", "target": "docs_audit_failures_indistinguishable_from_data", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_run_dev_entrypoint", "target": "readme_simulatedservorepository", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_adb_push_wipe_first", "target": "context_air_gapped_deploy